  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental data from the Total Governmental Funds column (pp5-6); business-type from Combined System Utilities Fund statement of revenues, expenses and changes in net position (p8) and cash flows (p9); measure recorded as cash (cash is the only asset). Beginning cash 549,767 = fund balances Sept 30, 2024 (restatement of 317,626 in General nets to zero across funds in the total column). Loan proceeds 28,082 are in debt_proceeds, not receipts; printed Total revenues 379,292 includes it. Transfers_in 110,499 is the net transfers printed in the total column (General fund transfers in 123,576 less Street 9,077 and Debt Service 4,000 out). Identity: 549,767 + 351,210 - 448,327 + 110,499 + 28,082 = 591,231. Business-type: 28,608 + 587,554 - 450,935 - 110,499 = 54,728. Business-type printed no single receipts/disbursements total; summed (computed). Attempt 2 (targeted re-check): balance sheet governmental lines now from the governmental funds Balance Sheet (p4, Total Governmental Funds column, fund balance by classification), since its total 591,231 equals the government-wide governmental column (p1); business-type lines and the overall totals 645,959 stay from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Utility 'Power' 274,382 recategorized as Purchased Power/Cost of Sales (utility cost type; power bought for resale in the combined utility). General Fund detail uses the departments combining schedule (p12-13, more detailed) instead of the General Fund budget schedule (p10); the Street Fund uses its budget schedule (p11); budget_final is null for the departments schedule. Departments schedule transfers are in other financing lines. Street schedule Total resources 121,521 includes loan proceeds 28,082. Debt Service, Library, Cemetery, Summer Sports funds have no separate schedule. Statement of cash flows (p9) is cash-basis, so proprietary is null. Read pages 1-13 of 13",
